args:
- description: Exception rule ID. Accepts a comma seperated list.
  disabled: false
  hidden: false
  isdetailsoverridden: false
  isgeneratable: false
  name: id
  required: false
  type: string
  underlyingargname: ids
- description: The rule name. Accepts a comma-separated list.
  disabled: false
  hidden: false
  isdetailsoverridden: false
  isgeneratable: false
  name: rule_name
  required: false
  type: string
  underlyingargname: rule_names
- description: |
    Platforms the rule applies to. Accepts a comma-separated list. Options: AGENT_OS_WINDOWS, AGENT_OS_MAC, AGENT_OS_LINUX, AGENT_OS_ANDROID, AGENT_OS_IOS, AGENT_OS_CAAS_LINUX, AGENT_OS_SERVERLESS.
  disabled: false
  hidden: false
  isdetailsoverridden: false
  isgeneratable: false
  name: platform
  required: false
  type: string
  underlyingargname: platforms
- description: Filter results by the provided value within the rule conditions. These
    conditions define the specific criteria required for an exception to apply. They
    act as a filter to narrow the scope, identifying specific entities—such as processes,
    files, IP addresses, hashes, or other relevant attributes—to be excluded from
    the affected module. Accepts a comma-separated list.
  disabled: false
  hidden: false
  isdetailsoverridden: false
  isgeneratable: false
  name: conditions
  required: false
  type: string
  underlyingargname: conditions
- description: The email address of the user that created the rule. Accepts a comma-separated
    list.
  disabled: false
  hidden: false
  isdetailsoverridden: false
  isgeneratable: false
  name: user_email
  required: false
  type: string
  underlyingargname: user_emails
- description: |
    The start time for filtering according to rule modification time. Supports free-text relative and absolute times. For example: 7 days ago, 2023-06-15T10:30:00Z, 13/8/2025. If start_modification_time is provided but not end_modification_time - end_modification_time will be set to current time.
  disabled: false
  hidden: false
  isdetailsoverridden: false
  isgeneratable: false
  name: start_modification_time
  required: false
  type: string
  underlyingargname: start_modification_time
- description: |
    The end time for filtering according to rule modification time. Supports free-text relative and absolute times. For example: 7 days ago, 2023-06-15T10:30:00Z, 13/8/2025. Must be used in conjunction with start_modification_time. If end_modification_time is provided but not start_modification_time - start_modification_time is set to 0.
  disabled: false
  hidden: false
  isdetailsoverridden: false
  isgeneratable: false
  name: end_modification_time
  required: false
  type: string
  underlyingargname: end_modification_time
- description: |
    The status of the exception rule. Options: ENABLED, DISABLED.
  disabled: false
  hidden: false
  isdetailsoverridden: false
  isgeneratable: false
  name: status
  required: false
  type: string
  underlyingargname: status
- description: |
    The type of the disable prevention rule. Accepts a comma-separated list. Options: XDR, WAAS.
  disabled: false
  hidden: false
  isdetailsoverridden: false
  isgeneratable: false
  name: rule_type
  required: false
  type: string
  underlyingargname: rule_types
- description: |
    The type of the exception rule. If not specified, both are returned. Options: legacy_agent_exceptions, disable_prevention_rules.
  disabled: false
  hidden: false
  isdetailsoverridden: false
  isgeneratable: false
  name: type
  required: false
  type: string
  underlyingargname: type
- defaultvalue: "100"
  description: Number of exception rules to return. Default is 100. Ignored if 'retrieve_all'
    is set to true.
  disabled: false
  hidden: false
  isdetailsoverridden: false
  isgeneratable: false
  name: page_size
  required: false
  type: string
  underlyingargname: page_size
- defaultvalue: "0"
  description: Page number to return. Default is 0. Ignored if 'retrieve_all' is set
    to true.
  disabled: false
  hidden: false
  isdetailsoverridden: false
  isgeneratable: false
  name: page
  required: false
  type: string
  underlyingargname: page
- defaultvalue: "true"
  description: Return all exception rules. Default is true.
  disabled: false
  hidden: false
  isdetailsoverridden: false
  isgeneratable: false
  name: retrieve_all
  required: false
  type: string
  underlyingargname: retrieve_all
